# Analysis dialogs. Radial distribution function: the first peak of fcc Cu
# (a = 3.61) at a/sqrt(2) = 2.553 A with 12 neighbours in the first shell;
# angular distribution of the first shell: peaks at 60, 90 and 120 degrees
# (180 lies in the last bin, which the peak finder does not report).
open docs/manual/examples/cu_fcc.cif
step replicate
set counts 3 3 3
apply
rdf open
rdf rmax 6
rdf bins 600
rdf distortion on
rdf run
expect-rdf peak 2.555
expect-rdf coordination 12
rdf pair Cu Cu
rdf run
expect-rdf peak 2.555
adf open
adf cutoff 3.0
adf run
expect-adf-peak 60
expect-adf-peak 90
expect-adf-peak 120
cna open
cna cutoff 3.0
cna run
expect-cna FCC-like 108
open docs/manual/examples/cu_ni_alloy.cif
sro open
sro shells 2
sro run
expect-sro 1 Cu Ni -0.0286
expect-sro 2 Cu Ni 0.0286
screenshot rust/target/ui/analysis.png
quit
